537-
538-When version comparison, release-readiness, or repeated workflow quality is the live problem:
539:- distinguish document completeness from measured behavior quality
540-- prefer benchmark-backed statements over comparative prose with no replay or eval support
541-- treat context sufficiency, critique quality, adaptation promotion, route quality, and verification-running discipline as separately reviewable control surfaces
542-- keep packet usage, omission findings, replay coverage, reviewer burden, and rollback signals explicit when they materially affect a release or promotion decision
