544-### 16.2 Executable-proof rule
545-
546-When the task depends on benchmarked or release-grade agentic proof:
547:- distinguish `benchmark registry` from `benchmark execution state`
548:- distinguish `replay surface` from `replay execution state`
549-- distinguish threshold language from a real `adaptation lifecycle state`
550-- distinguish coding plausibility from a `Coding proof bundle memo`
551-- keep `executed-vs-unexecuted` status explicit when command, test, or harness execution changes claim strength
552-- keep `release recommendation confidence class` explicit when promotion evidence remains partial
--
557-- distinguish a named packet from a linked run artifact with `scenario_id`, `run_id`, `cohort_id`, `trace_id`, or `artifact_version`
558-- distinguish a review memo from an execution ledger, verdict sheet, controller audit packet, or promotion decision record
559-- if the required packet floor for a replay, release, adaptation, or telemetry claim is missing, downgrade the claim before using stronger operational language
560-- if the required packet exists but the recommended companion is absent, keep the weaker companion-missing language explicit rather than silently using the stronger claim
561:- treat `Benchmark cohort manifest`, `Replay runner verdict sheet`, `Adaptation controller audit packet`, `Coding benchmark execution ledger`, `Release promotion decision record`, `Telemetry drift investigation memo`, `Route-switch benchmark verdict`, and `Context substrate scorecard` as the minimum operational floor before benchmark-grade, replay-grade, controller-grade, coding-proof-grade, release-grade, drift-grade, route-quality-grade, or retrieval-substrate-grade language
562-- when a stronger operational artifact exists for the same control problem, follow it and keep the lighter memo as background lookup or mark it superseded
563-- prefer one active artifact per control problem and make superseded lower-strength packets explicit rather than silently emitting both
564-- let a newer compatible artifact supersede a stale predecessor explicitly rather than keeping both active by inertia
565-- if multiple artifacts must be synthesized, keep one explicit join rule for precedence, compatibility, freshness, completeness, and downgrade behavior
566-- reject incompatible merges that would weaken a stronger artifact; preserve split verdicts, upstream source IDs, and `artifact_version` instead
567:- if operational evidence is absent, downgrade the claim before escalating to release, adaptation promotion, or telemetry-trend language
